operator's call stands), **arrow swipe-cue on ALL 5 slides** (including
slide 5, alongside its CTA badge).

**Link/topic source:** Reuses the SAME daily link rotation as Pinterest's
Nail Care Tips board — same link, same day, same topic across both
platforms. Formula: Day 1 = Aug 4 2026, `day_index = (days since Aug 4
2026) mod 256`, link at position `(day_index + 1)` in the master 256-link
list (see link_rotation_file_ in project files).

### Slide content rules — CRITICAL, caught and fixed during this build
- **Exact final copy must be written into every image-generation prompt,
  word-for-word, with an explicit "no rephrasing" instruction.** This was a
  hard lesson: writing prompts that let the image generator phrase its own
  text produces grammatical errors (e.g. "protects your nail as grows"
  instead of "as it grows"). Never let the generator improvise final
  wording.
- **Watermark (mirelleinspo.com) must be explicitly instructed to appear
  EXACTLY ONCE per slide.** Caught a duplicate-watermark bug on slide 5
  during testing — always state this explicitly in the prompt.
- Keep all text within upper 75-85% of canvas (bottom ~250px often
  obscured by mobile UI/caption).
- Slide 1 carries ~80% of the "hook" weight — bold headline (5-8 words),
  curiosity gap. Slide 2 must independently hook too (Instagram's
  "re-serve" mechanism shows slide 2 to people who scrolled past slide 1).
  One idea per slide. Consistent visual system (palette/fonts/layout)
  across all 5 slides.
- Last slide = single clear CTA badge/pill (e.g. "Read full guide ↓")

### Caption structure
- Hook line (mirrors slide 1) + literal arrow (↓) + "Read full guide" +
  the link as plain text (NOT clickable on IG — caption links are not
  clickable for feed posts/carousels except in a limited paid Meta Verified
  beta, not something to build a daily system around)
- FAQ-style: a direct question in the user's real search language, then a
  short direct answer
- Main long-tail keyword + one supporting query, each repeated naturally
  3-4 times across the caption
- No hashtags, ever
- Target length: 300-500 chars normal day, up to 800 if genuinely needed
  (first ~125 chars are what shows before "...more" — front-load the hook)
- Primary CTA mechanism is **bio link** (up to 5 links allowed on IG in
  2026), since caption links aren't reliably clickable — the "link in bio"
  phrase in the CTA badge/caption is intentional, not a placeholder.

### Research method (locked, confirmed by operator)
Use `site:mirelleinspo.com [exact-slug]` first. If the exact page doesn't
index (happens — confirmed inconsistent), infer the topic from the slug
name and research it properly on the open web — same depth of rigor,
never fall back to generic/invented content.

